{"id":"5c1106de-d8a5-4e54-a5a4-0224c9ba0e47","object":"chat.completion","created":1784990821,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"import math\\n\\ndef solve(case):\\n    matrix = case['matrix']\\n    idf = case['idf']\\n    vector = case['vector']\\n    \\n    n_rows = len(matrix)\\n    n_cols = len(matrix[0])\\n    \\n    # Scale matrix columns by IDF\\n    scaled = [[matrix[i][j] * idf[j] for j in range(n_cols)] for i in range(n_rows)]\\n    \\n    # Compute row degrees (squared norm) with positive floor\\n    eps = 1e-12\\n    degrees = []\\n    for i in range(n_rows):\\n        s = sum(scaled[i][j] ** 2 for j in range(n_cols))\\n        if s < eps:\\n            s = eps\\n        degrees.append(s)\\n    \\n    # Compute inverse sqrt of degrees\\n    inv_sqrt_deg = [1.0 / math.sqrt(d) for d in degrees]\\n    \\n    # Scale input vector by inverse sqrt degree\\n    v_scaled = [vector[i] * inv_sqrt_deg[i] for i in range(n_rows)]\\n    \\n    # Compute b = X^T * v_scaled\\n    b = [0.0] * n_cols\\n    for j in range(n_cols):\\n        total = 0.0\\n        for i in range(n_rows):\\n            total += scaled[i][j] * v_scaled[i]\\n        b[j] = total\\n    \\n    # Compute y = X * b\\n    y = [0.0] * n_rows\\n    for i in range(n_rows):\\n        total = 0.0\\n        for j in range(n_cols):\\n            total += scaled[i][j] * b[j]\\n        y[i] = total\\n    \\n    # Rescale rows by inverse sqrt degree again\\n    result = [y[i] * inv_sqrt_deg[i] for i in range(n_rows)]\\n    # Round result to avoid floating point noise (8 decimal places)\\n    result = [round(v, 8) for v in result]\\n    \\n    return {\\n        'degree': degrees,\\n        'result': result\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to parse the problem. The task is DATA-SNAP-02. The function solve(case) receives a payload with fields: matrix, idf, vector, _case_nonce. We need to compute something and return an o